AB  - The biomass, photosynthesis and respiration of microflora and algaflora of bottom sediments and periphyton were determined in the study of productivity of coastal coral reefs.  It was shown that bottom reef biotopes may produce 1-5 g organic carbon as a result of photosynthesis and heterotrophic biosynthesis.  This organic matter serves as an energetic basis for feeding of bottom fauna and being emanated to water from bottom biotopes is a very important source of energy for the plankton of tropical shelf coastal waters.
