FX  - We thank those who contributed to the success of the SS062008 survey, in particular the Captain and crew of the R/V Southern Surveyor and Cruise Chief Colin Woodroffe (University of Wollongong). Support with multibeam data processing was provided by C. Buchanan, M. Spinoccia, A. Cortese, R. Mleczko and J. Siwabessy (Geoscience Australia). Michelle Linklater (UOW) assisted with the geomorphic feature maps and Z. Huang (GA) provided several multibeam derived variables. We also thank the taxonomic experts who identified biological specimens from this collection: J. Lowry and L. Hughes (Amphipods), G. Wilson (Isopods), T. O'Hara (Echinoderms), R. Wilson (Polychaetes), and Jo Taylor (Carids); and M. Cappo and P. Speare for providing underwater images and conversations that assisted the preparation of this manuscript. N. Bax, N. Hill, Z. Huang and M. Tran provided valuable comments on the manuscript. This research was partially funded by the Australian Government's Commonwealth Environment Research Facilities (CERF) Marine Biodiversity Hub, and was undertaken as a collaboration between the University of Wollongong and Geoscience Australia using the Australian National Facility Vessel R/V Southern Surveyor, with permission from the Lord Howe Island Board, Lord Howe Island Marine Park Authority, and the Australian Department of the Environment, Water, Heritage and the Arts. Published with permission of the Chief Executive Officer, Geoscience Australia.
