FX  - Bathymetric, sediment and biological data were collected as part of the Offshore Energy Security Programme (2007-2011) funded by the Commonwealth Government of Australia. We thank the crew of RV Tangaroa for their technical support during survey TAN0713, and the field engineering and research staff from both NIWA and Geoscience Australia that participated in this survey. We also thank C. Buchanan and Michele Spinnocia for processing the multibeam bathymetry; J. Siwabessy for providing processed backscatter; Andrew Heap and Danielle Payne for their work on the geomorphic features map of Gifford Guyot; the Palaeontology and Sedimentology Laboratory at Geoscience Australia for sediment analyses; and the taxonomic experts who identified biological specimens from this collection: T. O'Hara (Asteroids, Echinoids, Ophiuroids), R. Wilson (Polchaetes), P. Allderslade, K. Miller, and K. Moore (Octocorallia), R. Webber, G. Poore and J. Lowry (Crustacea), B. Marshall (Mollusca), C. Battershill (Porifera), and M. McGrouther and M. Francis (Fishes). N. Bax (CERF Marine Biodiversity Hub) and three anonymous reviewers provided valuable comments on the manuscript. This paper is a contribution to the Australian Government's Commonwealth Environment Research Facilities (CERF) Marine Biodiversity Hub and is published with permission of the Chief Executive Officer, Geoscience Australia.
